Company Description
We are a Bosch company, but we do not produce tangible objects such as DIY tools or car parts. Service is our product. We provide services and complex technology driven solutions in the area Business Process Outsourcing, and this makes us unique in the Bosch world.  


We work with leading companies from the automotive, travel, tourism, building and telecommunications sectors across the world as well as other Bosch units. So besides having external client, we also work for the Bosch Group itself, helping colleagues and divisions in other areas.  

As part of the Bosch group, we operate in one of its four main business areas – the Building and Energy Technologies unit. There is a historical reason for it. We used to be part of Bosch Security Systems (producer of security hardware and security solutions). For them we managed for e.g. on-going product maintenance or the emergency and monitoring call center.

Job Description
We are seeking an organized, proactive, and people-centric People Operations & Workforce Administration Coordinator. In this role, you will play a central part in administrative personnel management, time and attendance tracking, workforce scheduling, and operational workflow follow-up.

Acting as the key bridge between operational teams and corporate departments—primarily Human Resources—you will not only guarantee operational compliance and data integrity, but also actively champion Bosch’s mission, vision, and core values. You will serve as an ambassador for an outstanding employee experience, fostering an inclusive, diverse environment and bringing positive energy and great vibes to our teams every day.

1. Culture, Diversity & Employee Experience Ambassadorship

Live & Promote Bosch Values: Embody and actively champion Bosch’s mission, values, and leadership principles across daily interactions and communications.

Employee Experience: Partner with HR to enhance the end-to-end employee journey, from seamless onboarding through regular workforce touchpoints.

2. Time & Attendance Management

Time Tracking & Validation: Conduct daily reviews and validation of time logs using BSO Manager and internal tracking systems, ensuring full alignment with shifts, absences, and planned schedules.

Discrepancy Resolution: Promptly identify, investigate, and correct discrepancies in hours logged versus scheduled shifts.

3. Leave & Absence Administration

Absence & Leave Coordination: Oversee the end-to-end administration of employee leaves, including annual vacations, public holiday compensations, and personal days.

Medical & Family Leave Follow-up: Track and manage documentation for medical leaves, parental leaves (maternity/paternity), and other statutory absences in full compliance with labor guidelines and company standards.

4. Operational Alignment & Cross-Functional Coordination

Operations Liaison: Conduct regular sync meetings with operational leads to review workforce management incidents, upcoming staffing requirements, and open administrative action items.

HR & Departmental Collaboration: Serve as the primary operational point of contact for Human Resources and related departments, ensuring fluid communication and swift closure of employee-related requests.

5. Administrative Tracking & Workforce Analytics

Personnel Record Maintenance: Keep master rosters, internal databases, headcount movements, new hires, and departures meticulously up to date.

Hours Analysis & Reporting: Monitor scheduled vs. actual hours per service/project, generate periodic control reports, and proactively flag trends or deviations to operational management.

Qualifications
Labour Law & Regulatory Knowledge: Basic understanding of Spanish labour law, including familiarity with applicable collective bargaining agreements (convenio colectivo) and statutory rules regarding working hours, leaves, and employee administration.

Mindset & Ownership: High sense of responsibility, proactive initiative, and a strong commitment to quality and accuracy.

End-to-End Problem Solver: Solution-oriented mindset with the drive to follow through and achieve definitive closure on open issues, rather than just executing transactional tasks.

Technical & Analytical Proficiency: Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and ease working with workforce management software, digital tools, and master control files.

Interpersonal & Communication Skills: Outstanding communication abilities with a collaborative, empathetic spirit and a natural orientation toward people management and team engagement.

Organizational Agility: Proven capacity to manage multiple competing priorities, operate with autonomy, and anticipate potential bottlenecks before they arise.

Desirable / Value-Added Qualifications

Languages: Professional working proficiency in English (capable of collaborating effectively in a multicultural/global environment), alongside fluency in Spanish.

Location: Preference for candidates based in Barcelona. 

